// expect: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// A NEGATIVE COUNT IS NO LENGTH: `make_list` handed its count straight to the
// allocator, whose overflow guard trapped as though memory were exhausted,
// and no row said so — `mk` checked clean under `!Trap` and `mk(0 - 5)`
// trapped (boot 3e60dafe). The count is the list's precondition, checked
// before anything is allocated, and a call carries the `Trap` it can raise.
fn mk(n) with !Trap = make_list(n)

fn main() = len(mk(3))
